---
// The workflow reference, the topic "workflow-reference" of the docs: every
// step of the workflow (src/lib/steps.ts) with what happens and its facts in
// the five fixed fields, by stage. It was "Every step in detail" on /workflow
// and then /docs/reference/workflow/, whose old anchors lead here. A compact
// index of the steps with their command and where it runs, and the
// parameters of the commands, come first (#335). Every id has the prefix of
// the topic, as the ids of the Markdown topics have (#373).
import Table from "./Table.astro";
import { parameters, parts as values, reference, stages } from "../lib/steps";

/** The id of the reference on the one docs page. */
const at = (id: string) => `workflow-reference/${id}`;
const fact = (facts: [string, string][], term: string) => facts.find(([t]) => t === term)?.[1];
---
<p>Look up a step here when you run it. <a href="#workflow-and-commands">How the workflow works</a> explains when to use which step and what to do when one stops.</p>

<h3 id={at("index")}>Step index</h3>
<p>Every step with its command and the checkout or worktree to run it from. Run each command from the root of that checkout. The primary checkout is the clone of your repository; the scripts create the planning and feature worktrees next to it and print their paths.</p>
<Table label="Step index">
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">step</th><th scope="col">command</th><th scope="col">run from</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    {stages.flatMap((stage) => stage.steps).map((step) => (
      <tr>
        <th scope="row"><a href={`#${at(step.id)}`}>{step.title}</a></th>
        <td data-col="command">{values(fact(step.facts, "script") ?? "—").map((v) => (v.code ? <code>{v.part}</code> : v.part))}</td>
        <td data-col="run from">{values(fact(step.facts, "where") ?? "—").map((v) => (v.code ? <code>{v.part}</code> : v.part))}</td>
      </tr>
    ))}
  </tbody>
</Table>

<h3 id={at("parameters")}>Parameters</h3>
<p>A word in angle brackets in a command is a parameter: replace it, brackets included, with your value. A parameter in square brackets may be left out.</p>
<dl class="facts">
  {parameters.map(([name, meaning]) => <><dt><code>{name}</code></dt><dd>{values(meaning).map((v) => (v.code ? <code>{v.part}</code> : v.part))}</dd></>)}
</dl>

{stages.map((stage) => <>
  <h3 id={at(stage.id)}>{stage.title}</h3>
  <p>{stage.note}</p>
  {stage.steps.map((step) => (
    <section class="ref-step" id={at(step.id)} aria-labelledby={at(`${step.id}-h`)}>
      <h4 id={at(`${step.id}-h`)}>{step.title}</h4>
      <p class="what">{values(step.text).map((v) => (v.code ? <code>{v.part}</code> : v.part))}</p>
      <dl class="ref-fields">
        {reference(step).map((row) => <>
          <dt>{row.label}</dt>
          <dd>{row.facts.length === 1 && !row.facts[0].shown
            ? values(row.facts[0].value).map((v) => (v.code ? <code>{v.part}</code> : v.part))
            : <ul>{row.facts.map((fact) => <li>{fact.shown && <><span class="sub">{fact.label}</span> </>}{values(fact.value).map((v) => (v.code ? <code>{v.part}</code> : v.part))}</li>)}</ul>}</dd>
        </>)}
      </dl>
    </section>
  ))}
</>)}
